ret = read_chunk_bytes(ctx, chunk.length);  // line 1051 - reads chunk data into ctx->data
if(ret) return ret;

// Now data is stale if realloc happened
if(!memcmp(chunk.type, type_exif, 4))
{
    // ...
    memcpy(exif.data, data, chunk.length);  // uses stale data!
}
```

But `read_chunk_bytes` reads the chunk data INTO `ctx->data`. After realloc, `ctx->data` points to new memory, and `data` points to the old (freed) memory. Then `data` is used to read the chunk data - but the chunk data was read into `ctx->data` (the new buffer), not `data` (the old buffer). So `data` contains garbage/old data.

Actually wait - in streaming mode, `read_data` does:
```c
